equired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Checks the text and returns an error message, or null to accept it.'), ApiParameter(name: 'required', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether an empty field shows the localized "This field is required"\nerror; a password of only spaces is not empty.')])], properties: [], methods: [], values: []),
  'Oito2PasswordHint': ApiEntry(kind: 'enum', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'A suggestion that makes a password stronger, given by\n[Oito2PasswordStrength.hints].', signature: '', constructors: [], properties: [], methods: [ApiMember(name: 'labelIn', signature: 'labelIn(Oito2Localizations strings) → String', doc: 'Returns the localized suggestion from [strings], such as "Add more\ncharacters".')], values: [ApiMember(name: 'avoidCommon', signature: '', doc: 'The password is one of the most common passwords or contains one.'), ApiMember(name: 'avoidPersonalInfo', signature: '', doc: 'The password contains the user\'s name, email or another given input.'), ApiMember(name: 'avoidWords', signature: '', doc: 'The password is a common English or Portuguese word or contains one.'), ApiMember(name: 'avoidDates', signature: '', doc: 'The password contains a year or a date.'), ApiMember(name: 'avoidSequences', signature: '', doc: 'The password contains a run such as "abcd", "4321" or "qwerty".'), ApiMember(name: 'avoidRepeats', signature: '', doc: 'The password repeats a character or a group, such as "aaaa" or\n"abab".'), ApiMember(name: 'addLength', signature: '', doc: 'The password is short.'), ApiMember(name: 'mixCharacters', signature: '', doc: 'The password uses only one or two kinds of characters.')]),
  'Oito2PasswordStrength': ApiEntry(kind: 'class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'How hard a password is to guess: a [level] from 0 (very weak) to 4\n(strong) and the [hints] that would make it stronger, most useful\nfirst.\n\n[estimate] rates a password on the device, without sending it\nanywhere. A field can take another estimator, such as a port of\nzxcvbn, that returns this value.', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2PasswordStrength', doc: 'Creates a strength of [level], from 0 to 4, with [hints].', isConst: true, isFactory: false, parameters: [ApiParameter(name: 'level', type: 'int', isRequired: true, isNamed: false, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The rating: 0 very weak, 1 weak, 2 fair, 3 good and 4 strong.'), ApiParameter(name: 'hints', type: 'List<Oito2PasswordHint>', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'const []', doc: 'The suggestions that would make the password stronger, most useful\nfirst; empty for a strong password.')])], properties: [], methods: [ApiMember(name: 'labelIn', signature: 'labelIn(Oito2Localizations strings) → String', doc: 'Returns the localized name of [level] from [strings], such as\n"Weak".'), ApiMember(name: 'estimate', signature: 'static estimate(String password, Iterable<String> userInputs) → Oito2PasswordStrength', doc: 'Rates [password] on the device with a heuristic.\n\nThe rating adds up the bits an attacker would need for each part of\nthe password: characters drawn from the kinds the password uses\n(lowercase, uppercase, digits, symbols and others) cost the most,\nwhile parts an attacker tries first cost little: one of about five\nhundred very common passwords, one of about thirteen hundred common\nEnglish and Portuguese words, a word of [userInputs] such as the\nuser\'s name or the parts of an email, a year or a date, an\nalphabetical, numeric or keyboard run, and repeated characters or\ngroups. Words are also found with accents removed and with\nlook-alike digits and symbols read as letters ("0" as "o", "1" as\n"i" or "l", "3" as "e", "4" and "@" as "a", "5" and "\$" as "s", "7"\nas "t", "8" as "b", "!" as "i" and "|" as "l"), whatever their case.\n\nA password that is a common password with at most six digits or\nsymbols before or after it, such as "Senha@2024", is level 0, and a\ncommon word with such affixes, such as "Montanha@77", is at most\nlevel 1. A password with a year or a date anywhere, not next to\nanother digit, such as "nascido em 1990", is at most level 2. Below\n8 characters the level is at most 1. The hints of every part found\nadd up, also for a common password, except the advice to mix kinds\nof characters, which doesn\'t help a common password.\n\nThis is a quick estimate, not a guarantee: a field can take a\nstronger estimator, such as a port of zxcvbn, that returns this\nvalue.\n\nEach character counts once, also one outside the Basic Multilingual\nPlane, such as an emoji.\n\nReturns level 0 without hints for an empty password.')], values: []),
  'Oito2PinEntry': ApiEntry(kind: 'class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'A code entry drawn as [length] one-character cells, such as a PIN or\na one-time code.\n\nOne text field sits under the cells, so typing, deleting, pasting a\nwhole code and one-time code autofill all work as in any field; a\npasted code fills the cells in order. When the last cell is filled the\nentry calls [onCompleted] and gives up the focus.\n\nThe error of [validator] or [required] shows below the cells after the\nentry loses focus, or at once after its [Oito2Form] found errors.', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2PinEntry', doc: 'Creates a code entry.\n\nThrows an [AssertionError] in debug mode when [length] is not greater\nthan zero.', isConst: true, isFactory: false, parameters: [ApiParameter(name: 'participatesInForm', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'true', doc: 'Whether the field registers with the closest [Oito2Form], taking\npart in its validation, error summary and dirty state; true by\ndefault. When false, the field shows its own errors as outside a\nform.'), ApiParameter(name: 'length', type: 'int', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '6', doc: 'The number of characters.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onChanged', type: 'ValueChanged<String>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called when the code changes.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onCompleted', type: 'ValueChanged<String>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called when every cell is filled.'), ApiParameter(name: 'numeric', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'true', doc: 'Whether only digits are accepted.'), ApiParameter(name: 'obscure', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether the characters show as dots.'), ApiParameter(name: 'hasError', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether the cells show the error border.'), ApiParameter(name: 'controller', type: 'TextEditingController?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The text controller; one is created when null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'focusNode', type: 'FocusNode?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The focus node; one is created when null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'autofocus', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether the entry takes the focus when shown.'), ApiParameter(name: 'enabled', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'true', doc: 'Whether the entry accepts input.'), ApiParameter(name: 'semanticLabel', type: 'String?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The accessibility label; defaults to a description of the code\nlength.'), ApiParameter(name: 'validator', type: 'String? Function(String)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Checks the code and returns an error message, or null to accept it.'), ApiParameter(name: 'required', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether an empty entry shows the localized "This field is required"\nerror.')])], properties: [], methods: [], values: []),
  'Oito2PlaceholderIcon': ApiEntry(kind: 'class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'A decorative square that stands in for a missing picture, such as an\nalbum cover or an app icon that has not loaded.\n\nIt fills a rounded square with a container tone of the color scheme\nand draws a picture outline in its center. It is hidden from assistive\ntechnologies.', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2PlaceholderIcon', doc: 'Creates a placeholder icon.', isConst: true, isFactory: false, parameters: [ApiParameter(name: 'size', type: 'double', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '48', doc: 'The width and height.'), ApiParameter(name: 'borderRadius', type: 'BorderRadius', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'Oito2Radius.mediumAll', doc: 'The corner rounding.')])], properties: [], methods: [], values: []),
  'Oito2Platform': ApiEntry(kind: 'class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'Describes the platform an app runs on and the ergonomics that follow\nfrom it.\n\n[Oito2Platform.current] reads the running platform. The default\nconstructor accepts explicit values so tests and previews can simulate\nany platform.', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2Platform', doc: 'Creates a platform description from explicit values.', isConst: true, isFactory: false, parameters: [ApiParameter(name: 'targetPlatform', type: 'TargetPlatform', isRequired: true, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The operating system, or the browser host operating system on the web.'), ApiParameter(name: 'isWeb', type: 'bool', isRequired: true, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Whether the app runs inside a web browser.')]), ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2Platform.current', doc: 'Creates a platform description for the running app.\n\nReads [kIsWeb] and [defaultTargetPlatform], so it honors\n`debugDefaultTargetPlatformOverride`. On the web, [targetPlatform] is\nthe operating system of the browser host.', isConst: false, isFactory: true, parameters: [])], properties: [ApiMember(name: 'isDesktopNative', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the app runs as a native desktop app (Linux, Windows or\nmacOS), outside a browser.'), ApiMember(name: 'isTouch', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the app runs as a native app on a touch-first operating system\n(Android, iOS or Fuchsia), outside a browser.'), ApiMember(name: 'isWebTouch', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the app runs in a browser on a touch-first operating system.'), ApiMember(name: 'usesTouchInput', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the primary input is touch, natively or in a browser.'), ApiMember(name: 'isLinux', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the operating system is Linux.'), ApiMember(name: 'isWindows', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the operating system is Windows.'), ApiMember(name: 'isMacOS', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the op