  'Oito2TreeNode': ApiEntry(kind: 'class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'A node of an [Oito2TreeCollection]: a unique [value], a [label], an\noptional payload and, for branches, its [children].', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2TreeNode', doc: 'Creates a node; give [children] (possibly empty) to make a branch.\nThe [label] defaults to [value].', isConst: true, isFactory: false, parameters: [ApiParameter(name: 'value', type: 'String', isRequired: true, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The unique value of the node in its tree.'), ApiParameter(name: 'label', type: 'String?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: ''), ApiParameter(name: 'data', type: 'T?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The payload, such as the file or record the node shows.'), ApiParameter(name: 'children', type: 'List<Oito2TreeNode<T>>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The child nodes of a branch; null for a leaf.'), ApiParameter(name: 'disabled', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether the node can\'t be selected or focused.')])], properties: [ApiMember(name: 'isBranch', signature: 'bool', doc: 'Whether the node can have children.')], methods: [ApiMember(name: 'copyWith', signature: 'copyWith(String? label, T? data, List<Oito2TreeNode<T>>? children, bool? disabled) → Oito2TreeNode<T>', doc: 'Returns a copy with the given fields replaced; the [value] stays the\nsame, and [data] and [children] can\'t be reset to null this way.')], values: []),
  'Oito2TreeView': ApiEntry(kind: 'class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'A tree of the nodes of [collection], with open, selected and checked\nnodes kept in [controller].\n\nOnly the rows in view are built, so it handles large trees. The tree\ntakes the focus as a whole and marks its active row:\n\n- Up, Down, Home and End move the active row; a single-selection tree\n  selects it, and Shift extends a multiple selection.\n- Right opens a branch or moves to its first child; Left closes it or\n  moves to the parent.\n- Space toggles the check box of a [checkable] tree, or else the\n  selection of a multiple-selection one; Control+A (Command+A) selects\n  every shown, enabled node of a multiple-selection tree.\n- The Menu key or Shift+F10 calls [onContextMenu] for the active row,\n  as a secondary click does for the row under the pointer.\n- Enter, or a double click, calls [onActivate], or opens or closes a\n  branch when it is null.\n- F2 starts an inline rename of the active node when [onRename] is\n  set; Enter or leaving the field confirms it and Escape cancels it.\n- Typing letters jumps to the next shown label that starts with them.\n- With [onMove], Alt with Up or Down moves the active node before its\n  previous sibling or after its next one, Alt with Right (Left in\n  right-to-left layouts) moves it into the branch above it as its last\n  child, and Alt with Left moves it out of its branch, after it.\n\nWith [onMove], rows can also be dragged: with a mouse once it moves a\nfew pixels, and with a touch after a long press when [onContextMenu]\nis null; with [dragHandle], only a grip at the end of the label\ndrags, with any pointer, which leaves the long press to the context\nmenu. A drag carries the multiple selection when it starts on a\nselected row, and that row alone otherwise. The pointer\'s place in the\nrow under it picks the drop: the top quarter of a branch drops before\nit, the bottom quarter after it and the middle into it, as its last\nchild; a leaf takes the top or the bottom half. A drop after an open\nbranch with shown children goes in as its first child. A line between\nthe rows, at the depth the nodes will have, or a frame around the\ntarget branch shows the drop; a closed branch held under the pointer\nfor 700 milliseconds opens, loading its children as a click does, and\nthe tree scrolls when the pointer nears its top or bottom edge. A drop\ninto a dragged node or one of its descendants, or one [canDrop]\nrefuses, shows a "no drop" sign and calls nothing; Escape cancels the\ndrag. The tree doesn\'t change [collection]: the app moves the nodes,\nsuch as with [Oito2TreeCollection.move]. Rows can\'t be dragged or moved\nwhile filtering or renaming.\n\nA branch with no children yet and an [onLoadChildren] shows a spinner\nwhile its children load the first time it opens. A non-empty [query]\nshows only the matching nodes and their ancestors, all open, with the\nmatch highlighted; branches can\'t be opened or closed while filtering.\n\nA [checkable] tree derives a branch\'s check box from its leaves in\n[Oito2TreeController.checked] by default. With [checkState], the app\nowns the check states instead: the tree shows what it returns, and a\nclick or Space only calls [onCheckChanged], so a branch whose children\naren\'t loaded yet can show as checked or mixed.\n\nWith [columns], the tree is a tree grid: the first column holds the\nindentation, disclosure, check box, icon and label of each row, the\nother columns show cells aligned across every depth, and a header row\nwith the column labels stays above the rows.\nAs in an [Oito2DataTable], the user can hide and move the other\ncolumns through the header with [onHiddenColumnsChanged] and\n[onColumnsReordered], reset them with [onResetColumns], and\n[pinnedColumns] keeps the first ones in place while the rest scroll\nsideways. The first column always shows first: it can\'t be hidden or\nmoved.', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2TreeView', doc: 'Creates a tree view.', isConst: true, isFactory: false, parameters: [ApiParameter(name: 'collection', type: 'Oito2TreeCollection<T>', isRequired: true, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The nodes of the tree.'), ApiParameter(name: 'controller', type: 'Oito2TreeController', isRequired: true, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The open, selected and checked nodes.'), ApiParameter(name: 'itemBuilder', type: 'Oito2TreeItemBuilder<T>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Builds a row\'s content; the node label by default.'), ApiParameter(name: 'iconBuilder', type: 'Widget? Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>, bool)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Builds the icon before the label, given whether the node is open;\nno icon shows when it returns null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onActivate', type: 'ValueChanged<Oito2TreeNode<T>>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called on Enter or a double click on a node; when null, those open\nor close a branch instead.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onLoadChildren', type: 'Future<void> Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Loads the children of an empty branch the first time it opens; the\napp adds them to [collection].\n\nWhen the future fails, the error is reported through\n[FlutterError.reportError] and the branch closes; opening it again\nretries the load. [Oito2TreeController.reloadChildren] makes a\nloaded branch load again.\n\nNodes dropped or moved with the keyboard into a branch that hasn\'t\nloaded yet wait for the load and go after the loaded children.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onRename', type: 'void Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>, String)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called with a node and its new, trimmed label when a rename is\nconfirmed with a non-empty label that differs from the old one; F2\nrenames nothing when null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'checkable', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether the rows have tristate check boxes, tracked in\n[Oito2TreeController.checked].'), ApiParameter(name: 'query', type: 'String', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '\'\'', doc: 'The text that filters the nodes; blank shows the whole tree.'), ApiParameter(name: 'rowHeight', type: 'double?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The row height; defaults to the control height.'), ApiParameter(name: 'indent', type: 'double', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '16', doc: 'The indent of each level, in logical pixels.'), ApiParameter(name: 'semanticLabel', type: 'String?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The accessibility label of the tree.'), ApiParameter(name: 'autofocus', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether the tree takes the focus when shown.'), ApiParameter(name: 'checkState', type: 'bool? Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Returns the check state of a node in a [checkable] tree: true, false,\nor null for mixed; when set, it replaces the states derived from\n[Oito2TreeController.checked], which the tree then leaves untouched.\n\nIt is called only for the rows being built, so it must be cheap.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onCheckChanged', type: 'void Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>, bool)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called with a node and its next check state when its check box is\nclicked or Space is pressed on it, while [checkState] is set: true\nwhen it is unchecked or mixed, false when it is checked. Nothing else\nchanges; the app updates what [checkState] returns.'), ApiParameter(name: 'isPending', type: 'bool Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Whether a node has a change not applied yet; such rows show a small\ndot after the label and a "pending change" hint to assistive\ntechnologies.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onContextMenu', type: 'void Function(Oito2TreeNode<T>, Offset, bool)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called with a node, a global position and whether the keyboard\nasked for the menu: on a secondary click or a long press on its row,\nwith the pointer position and `byKeyboard` false, and on the Menu key\nor Shift+F10 for the active row, with the bottom-start corner of that\nrow and `byKeyboard` true.\n\nThe row becomes active first and is selected: alone in a single\nselection, and in a multiple selection unless it is already part of\nit. Disabled rows don\'t call it. An [Oito2ContextMenuRegion] with an\n[Oito2ContextMenuController] around the tree can open its menu at\nthe position, focusing its first item when `byKeyboard` is true.'), ApiParameter(name: 'columns', type: 'List<Oito2TableColumn<Oito2TreeNode<T>>>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The columns of a tree grid; null or empty shows the plain tree.\n\nThe first column shows the tree\'s own row content, or what its\n[Oito2TableColumn.cellBuilder] builds in place of the label when\n[itemBuilder] is null. Columns wider in total than the tree scroll\nsideways.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onColumnResized', type: 'void Function(String, double)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called with a column id and its new width when a resize of that\ncolumn ends; the app can keep the width and pass it back as an\n[Oito2ColumnWidth.fixed] width.'), ApiParameter(name: 'showHeader', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'true', doc: 'Whether a tree with [columns] shows the header row.'), ApiParameter(name: 'pinnedColumns', type: 'int', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '0', doc: 'How many shown [columns], from the start, stay in place while the\nothers scroll sideways, with a divider after them once the tree has\nscrolled; at most all but the last shown column.'), ApiParameter(name: 'hiddenColumns', type: 'Set<String>', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'const {}', doc: 'The ids of the [columns] the tree doesn\'t show; the first column\nalways shows, so its id is ignored.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onHiddenColumnsChanged', type: 'ValueChanged<Set<String>>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called with the ids of the columns to hide when the user shows or\nhides a column through the header menu, as\n[Oito2DataTable.onHiddenColumnsChanged]; the first column can\'t be\nhidden. The columns can\'t be hidden when null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'columnOrder', type: 'List<String>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The order of the [columns], by id, as [Oito2DataTable.columnOrder];\nthe first column always comes first, so its id is ignored.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onColumnsReordered', type: 'ValueChanged<List<String>>?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called with the ids of all the columns in their new order when the\nuser moves a column, as [Oito2DataTable.onColumnsReordered]; the\nfirst column can\'t move, and no column moves before it. The columns\ncan\'t be moved when null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'onResetColumns', type: 'VoidCallback?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called when the user picks "Reset columns" in the header menu, which\nshows that item only when this is set; the app puts back its own\ndefault [hiddenColumns] and [columnOrder].'), ApiParameter(name: 'onMove', type: 'void Function(List<Oito2TreeNode<T>>, String?, int)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Called when nodes are dragged to a new place, or the active node is\nmoved with the keyboard or an accessibility action, with the moved\nnodes in tree order, the value of their new parent (null for the top\nlevel) and their index among its children counted after the moved\nnodes are taken out of their places, as\n[Oito2TreeCollection.move] takes it; rows can\'t be moved when null.\n\nOnly the topmost of the dragged nodes are given: a node brings its\ndescendants along. Drops that leave the tree unchanged call nothing.'), ApiParameter(name: 'canDrop', type: 'bool Function(List<Oito2TreeNode<T>>, String?, int)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Returns whether [onMove] may move the nodes to the parent and index\nit would receive; every place but a dragged node and its descendants\nis allowed when null.\n\nIt is called as the pointer moves during a drag, so it must be cheap.'), ApiParameter(name: 'rowDropTargetBuilder', type: 'Widget Function(BuildContext, Oito2TreeNode<T>, Widget)?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'Wraps the row of each node, as built, such as in a [DragTarget] for\nthe app\'s own drags or a file drop target, to receive drops from\noutside the tree on a row; the row is returned unchanged when null.\n\nOnly the rows in view are built and wrapped. The tree\'s own row drags\ndon\'t use [DragTarget]s, so they never reach these targets.'), ApiParameter(name: 'dropHighlight', type: 'String?', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: '', doc: 'The value of a node to mark as the target of a drop from outside the\ntree, with the frame of a drop into a branch, such as while a\n[rowDropTargetBuilder] target is hovered; none when null.'), ApiParameter(name: 'dragHandle', type: 'bool', isRequired: false, isNamed: true, defaultValue: 'false', doc: 'Whether only a grip drags a row, instead of the whole row, when\n[onMove] is set.\n\nThe grip sits at the end of the row\'s label, inside the first column\nof a tree grid, so the other columns stay aligned with the header.\nAny pointer drags it at once, and on touch platforms it is padded to\na 48-pixel touch target as far as the row height allows; a long\npress on the row stays free for [onContextMenu].')])], properties: [], methods: [], values: []),
  'Oito2Typography': ApiEntry(kind: 'abstract class', package: 'oito2_ui', doc: 'Typography tokens: the bundled Inter font and the oito2 [TextTheme].', signature: '', constructors: [ApiConstructor(name: 'Oito2Typography', doc: '', isConst: false, isFactory: false, parameters: [])], properties: [ApiMember(name: 'fontFamily', signature: 'static String', doc: 'The font family name of Inter, as bundled by this package.\n\nUse it directly as `TextStyle.fontFamily`; it already carries the\npackage prefix, so don\'t pass `package: \'oito2_ui\'` along with it.'), ApiMember(name: 'fontFamilyFallback', signature: 'static List<String>', doc: 'System font families used for glyphs Inter lacks, in order.'), ApiMember(name: 'bodyLargeSize', signature: 'static double', doc: 'Font size of [TextTheme.bodyLarge]: 16.'), ApiMember(name: 'bodyMediumSize', signature: 'static double', doc: 'Font size of [TextTheme.bodyMedium]: 14.'), ApiMember(name: 'bodySmallSize', signature: 'static double', doc: 'Font size of [TextTheme.bodySmall]: 12.'), ApiMember(name: 'emphasisWeight', signature: 'static FontWeight', doc: 'Weight applied to headlines, titles and [TextTheme.labelLarge].')], methods: [ApiMember(name: 'textTheme', signature: 'static textTheme(Brightness brightness) → TextTheme', doc: 'Returns the oito2 text theme for [brightness].\n\nStarts from the Material 2021 typography (white glyphs for dark,\nblack glyphs for light), sets [fontFamily] and [fontFamilyFallback] on\nevery style, sets the body sizes to 16, 14 and 12, and applies\n[emphasisWeight] to every headline and title style and to\n[TextTheme.labelLarge].')], values: []),
